2 Invoking 'flow'
*****************

Synopsis:

     flow [options...]

2.1 'flow' Command-Line Options
===============================

'-file PATH|URI'
     Path or URI to XML file containing scripts, databases, and workflow
     nodes.  Default: 'scripts.xml'.

'-options PATH|URI'
     Path or URI to an XML CLI options defaults file
     ('<flow_cli_options><options>...').  Explicit CLI flags override
     values defined in '-options'.

'-config PATH|URI'
     Optional path or URI to a 'CONFIG.xml' file containing variable and
     database connection overrides merged with the base pipeline file.

'-format FORMAT'
     Output formatting for execution results: 'csv' (default), 'text',
     'json', 'jsonpretty' ('prettyjson'), 'markdown' ('md', 'table'), or
     'stream'.

'-vars KEY=VALUE[,...]'
     Comma-separated runtime variable overrides.  Recursively expands
     '{{var}}' placeholders up to 3 levels deep.

'-validate'
     Validate XML schema (XSD if '-xsd' is set) and AST semantic
     structure without executing pipeline nodes.

'-preflight'
     Execute only '<preflight>' validation nodes, skipping '<flow>'.

'-xsd PATH'
     Path to an '.xsd' schema file validated via 'xmllint' prior to
     parsing.

'-node-output'
     When logging to a database ('log_db'), persist redacted
     'ResultsString' values to 'pipeline_events.node_output' on
     'node.finished' rows.  Default: 'false'.

'-debug'
     Enable verbose console logging (connection resolution, dialect
     detection, signature metadata, and sink telemetry).

'-gopath DIR'
     GOPATH directory for dynamic package imports in the Yaegi Go
     interpreter.  Defaults to 'GOPATH'.

'-xslt PATH'
     Transform pipeline XML using a custom XSLT stylesheet with an
     auto-generated Mermaid workflow diagram, then exit.

'-out PATH'
     Output file path for XSLT-transformed XML produced by '-xslt'.

'-encrypted'
     Decrypt AES-256-GCM encrypted inputs prior to parsing, or encrypt
     items written by '-export-file' / '-import-file'.

'-secure-key KEY'
     Symmetric encryption/decryption passphrase or key (warns on
     'stderr').

'-key-file PATH'
     Path to file containing the symmetric key/passphrase.

'-verify-signature'
     Enforce digital signature verification before decrypting or
     executing.

'-public-key PATH'
     PEM public key file (RSA, ECDSA, Ed25519) for signature
     verification.

'-cert PATH'
     X.509 certificate file (PEM or DER) for PKCS#7/CMS or X.509
     verification.

'-ca-cert PATH'
     Root or intermediate CA certificate file for chain validation.

'-keyring PATH'
     OpenPGP armored public keyring file for GPG verification.

'-signature PATH'
     Detached digital signature file ('.sig', '.asc', '.p7s').
     Companion files with matching basenames are checked automatically
     when omitted.

'-builder'
     Start the local HTMX visual pipeline builder web server.

'-builder-port PORT'
     TCP port for the builder web server (default '0' selects an
     ephemeral port; falls back to 'FLOW_BUILDER_PORT' or 'PORT').

'-builder-db PATH'
     SQLite database path for visual builder local storage.  Default:
     'flow_builder.db'.

'-purge-db'
     Purge all data from the SQLite visual builder database,
     re-initialize defaults, and exit.

'-import-file PATH|URI'
     Import a pipeline, options, or config XML file into the SQLite
     builder DB or external DB ('-dsn').

'-import-name NAME'
     Custom record name for '-import-file' (defaults to file basename).

'-import-type TYPE'
     Item type for '-import-file': 'pipeline' (default), 'options', or
     'config'.

'-export-file PATH'
     Destination path to export a record (or '-' for 'stdout').  Disk
     files are written with '0600' permissions.

'-export-name NAME'
     Name of the record to export (required with '-export-file').

'-export-type TYPE'
     Item type for '-export-file': 'pipeline' (default), 'options', or
     'config'.

'-dsn DSN'
     External database DSN for repository import/export ('sqlserver',
     'postgres', 'mysql', 'sqlite').

2.2 'flow' Environment Variables
================================

   * 'FLOW_SECURE_KEY', 'SECURE_KEY': Symmetric passphrase.
   * 'FLOW_BUILDER_PORT', 'PORT': Default TCP port for '-builder'.
   * 'GOPATH': Go workspace directory for Yaegi package imports.
   * 'USER' / 'USERNAME', 'HOSTNAME' / 'COMPUTERNAME': Captured in
     'pipeline_runs' audit logs.

