6 '<pipeline>' XML Reference
****************************

The '<pipeline>' element is the root container of a Flow workflow
document.  Attribute names are case-insensitive and accept 'snake_case',
'kebab-case', and dot ('.') separators.  String values support
'{{VariableName}}' interpolation.

* Menu:

* Databases and Pools::         '<databases>' and '<database>'.
* Variables Section::           '<variables>' and '<variable>'.
* Preflight and Flow::          '<preflight>' and '<flow>'.
* Control Flow Elements::       '<foreach>', '<group>', '<while>', '<if>', '<parallel>'.
* Task Elements::               Templates, SQL, KV, Assertions, File/Excel I/O, Path queries, HTTP.

File: flow.info,  Node: Databases and Pools,  Next: Variables Section,  Prev: Pipeline XML Reference,  Up: Pipeline XML Reference

6.1 '<databases>' and '<database>'
==================================

'<databases>' is an optional container of '<database>' connection
definitions:

'name'
     (Mandatory) Unique handle referenced by 'db', 'database', or
     'target_db'.
'driver / type'
     Relational SQL ('sqlserver' [default], 'postgres', 'mysql',
     'sqlite', 'oracle') or Key-Value ('bbolt'/'bolt', 'badger',
     'redis'/'valkey', 'etcd').
'connection_string'
     (Mandatory) Driver DSN, URL, or path (supports '{{VariableName}}').
'workload'
     Pool tuning profile:
        * 'oltp' (default): 'max_open_conns=25', 'max_idle_conns=10',
          'conn_max_lifetime=5m', 'conn_max_idle_time=2m'.
        * 'bulk': '50' / '25' / '30m' / '10m'.
        * 'analytics': '15' / '8' / '30m' / '10m'.
        * 'batch': '20' / '10' / '15m' / '5m'.
'max_open_conns, max_idle_conns'
     Explicit pool size overrides ('max_idle_conns' is clamped to
     'max_open_conns').
'conn_max_lifetime_seconds / conn_max_lifetime'
     Connection reuse lifetime (duration string like '5m' or seconds).
'conn_max_idle_time_seconds / conn_max_idle_time'
     Idle connection timeout before closing (duration string like '2m'
     or seconds).
'id, description'
     Optional identifier and human-readable description.

File: flow.info,  Node: Variables Section,  Next: Preflight and Flow,  Prev: Databases and Pools,  Up: Pipeline XML Reference

6.2 '<variables>' and '<variable>'
==================================

'<variables>' declares initial typed variables via '<variable>':

'name'
     (Mandatory) Variable identifier for '{{VariableName}}'
     interpolation.
'value'
     (Mandatory) Initial value parsed according to 'type'.
'type'
     'string' (default), 'int'/'integer', 'bool'/'boolean',
     'float'/'double'/'float64', 'datetime', or 'date'.
'id, description'
     Optional metadata attributes.

File: flow.info,  Node: Preflight and Flow,  Next: Control Flow Elements,  Prev: Variables Section,  Up: Pipeline XML Reference

6.3 '<preflight>' and '<flow>'
==============================

   * '<preflight>': Optional setup, smoke-test, and connectivity
     validation container appearing once before '<flow>'.  Executed
     standalone via 'flow -preflight'.
   * '<flow>': Main execution container.  Child steps run sequentially
     in document order unless wrapped in '<parallel>', '<foreach>', or
     '<while>'.

File: flow.info,  Node: Control Flow Elements,  Next: Task Elements,  Prev: Preflight and Flow,  Up: Pipeline XML Reference

6.4 Control Flow and Logical Grouping
=====================================

'<foreach>'
     Runs nested child steps once per row returned by a SQL driver query
     on 'db'/'database' (inline SQL or 'var'/'variable').  Exposes
     columns in original, lowercase, and uppercase names, and sets
     'LOOP_INDEX' (zero-based) on each iteration.

'<group>'
     Sequential block supporting conditional execution ('var'/'if_var',
     'equals'/'val'/'value'/'if_val'/'if_equals', 'condition'/'cond'),
     database transactions ('transaction="true"' or 'tx="true"' on
     'db'), pinned database sessions ('session="true"',
     'pin_connection', 'pin_conn', 'sticky' to retain '#Temp' / 'CREATE
     TEMP TABLE' objects across steps), and context deadlines
     ('timeout', e.g. '30s', '5m').

'<while>'
     Repeats nested child steps while its condition holds, up to
     'max_iterations'/'max_loops' (default '1000').  Sets 'WHILE_INDEX'
     on each iteration.

'<if>, <then>, <else>'
     Evaluates condition attributes on '<if>'; runs '<then>' (or direct
     inline child nodes) when true and '<else>' when false.

'<parallel>'
     Runs nested child nodes concurrently across a goroutine pool
     controlled by 'max_threads'/'threads'/'concurrency' (default '0' =
     unbounded).  Thread-isolated variable snapshots merge safely on
     completion with collision namespacing ('WORKER_<id>_<key>').

File: flow.info,  Node: Task Elements,  Prev: Control Flow Elements,  Up: Pipeline XML Reference

6.5 Pipeline Task Elements
==========================

Most data-producing steps write to 'LAST_OUTPUT' as well as any
specified output variable.

'<template> / <template_html>'
     Render Go 'text/template' or XSS-safe 'html/template' from 'file'
     or inline body.  Attributes: 'id' (mandatory), 'name', 'file',
     'engine', 'output_var'/'var', 'mode' ('summary' or rendered text).

'<sql>'
     Execute SQL on 'db'/'database' from 'var'/'variable' or inline
     body; store result in 'output_var'/'out_var'/'output_variable'.

'<sql_bulk>'
     Stream rows from 'db'/'database' into 'target_table' on
     'target_db'/'target_database' (defaults to source 'db').  Uses
     native TDS 'CopyIn' for SQL Server ('tablock', 'check_constraints',
     'fire_triggers', 'keep_nulls') and prepared multi-row batched
     'INSERT' statements for PostgreSQL, MySQL, Oracle, and SQLite.
     Optional 'batch_size' and 'output_var'/'out_var'.

'<kv>'
     Atomic Key-Value operations ('get', 'put'/'set', 'delete'/'del',
     'scan'/'list') against 'db' in 'bucket' (default 'default') via
     attributes ('op', 'key', 'value') or inline DSL text.

'<kv_bulk>'
     Stream SQL query rows (col 1 = key, col 2 = value) from 'db' into
     KV 'target_db' and 'target_bucket'/'bucket' in batches
     ('batch_size' default '10000').

'<assert>'
     Check 'var' against 'equals'/'value'.  On failure, optionally set
     'fail_var' to 'fail_val' (default 'true'), run nested
     '<on_failure>' steps, and apply 'on_failure' ('halt' [default],
     'warn', or 'continue').

'<file_read> / <file_save>'
     Read 'file'/'path'/'filename' into 'var'/'output_var', or write
     'var'/inline body to disk ('append="true"' appends; parent
     directories are created automatically).

'<excel_write> / <excel_read>'
     Create/update 'file' ('.xlsx', 'sheet' default 'Sheet1') from SQL
     on 'db', or read a worksheet ('header="true"' default) as a JSON
     array into 'output_var'/'var'.

'<json_path> / <yaml_path> / <xml_xpath>'
     Extract data from 'file' or 'var' into 'output_var'/'out_var':
        * '<json_path>': 'path'/'jsonpath'; 'mode' = 'value' (default),
          'json', 'json_array'.
        * '<yaml_path>': 'path'/'yamlpath'; 'mode' = 'value' (default),
          'json', 'json_array', 'yaml'.
        * '<xml_xpath>': 'xpath'; 'mode' = 'text' (default), 'xml',
          'json_array'.

'<http_client>'
     Execute HTTP requests against 'uri'/'url' ('method' default 'GET',
     'data'/inline body, 'headers', 'content_type').  Stores body in
     'var'/'output_var' and status code in
     'status_code_var'/'status_var'.  Supports 'timeout',
     'follow_redirects', 'max_redirects', 'cookie_jar', 'proxy', TLS
     options ('tls_insecure_skip_verify', 'tls_handshake_timeout',
     'tls_server_name', 'tls_min_version', 'tls_max_version'), and
     transport pool tuning ('max_idle_conns', 'max_idle_conns_per_host'
     [default '10'], 'max_conns_per_host', 'idle_conn_timeout',
     'response_header_timeout', 'expect_continue_timeout',
     'max_response_header_bytes', 'write_buffer_size',
     'read_buffer_size', 'force_attempt_http2').

